comments:
Doing a quick search and I understand the situation. Win 10 has [Waitable Timer](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/sync/waitable-timer-objects) which is efficient and precise, but we need to support Win 7, so a loop with `YieldProcessor()` is used, hoping it will release CPU. (seems not work on my computer)

I'd suggest use Waitable Timer for Win 10 and above, use busy wait only for Win 7.

