@YYF233333 
Frame-rate locking was not stable. For example, locking to 30FPS on a 60Hz+ display would give an unstable frame-rate and cause jittering. A smooth locked 30FPS is a much better experience than an unsmooth 30FPS.

The previous sleep logic was not accurate, and was miss the refresh interval leading to the jittery frame-pacing.

